  "about": "Real pull requests with defects that other reviewers reported and the author fixed or confirmed. Lines are head-side at the reviewed commit. A finding matches a defect when it overlaps a location (and mentions one of `keys`, when given) or when its text matches every group in `terms`. `confirmed` defects score recall; `plausible` ones were reported but never confirmed and count as neither TP nor FP; `neutral` entries are findings the author declined, which count as known false positives, as do `invalid` entries checked by hand and found incorrect. `nit` entries are reported separately, not as recall or known false positives. `valid` entries are defects first reported by Revera evaluation runs and checked by hand against the code; they count as correct extras, not recall. `bodies/` holds each PR description as its author wrote it, without the summaries other review bots added later, since those name defects and later fixes.",
